The prescribed reply says an object that lacks `started_at` and `limit_seconds` raises, and the detached child exits in `next_action` without starting phase A. `next_action` returns `phase-a` when `check_version` is missing or not 1, and it does not read those fields. `{"status": "started"}` starts phase A. `check_line` still raises `KeyError` on that object. A `try`/`except` only in `check_line` would change probe for that object. There is no child exit on that object.

